Yes, that's right.  I'm glad you enjoyed that aspect of the post, and
I would appreciate a continued discussion of that issue.  However, I
would go farther than that, and say that I do not necessarily consider
"government and media" to be two separate entities.  During at least
one of the military "police actions" carried out by this country
during the past 25 years, it was commonly felt that the media were
being "manipulated from Moscow", although that was simply a euphemism
indicating a popular (i.e. "pro-war") opinion that the media were too
"liberal" in their viewpoint (i.e. they were "anti-war").  Currently,
I have felt that there are many discrepancies and inconsistencies
between (1) what I can plainly see with my own eyes, (2) what the
media reported a year ago, and (3) what the media report today,
concerning the Waco events and other current issues (e.g. Presidential
impropriety and financial criminality).  Therefore, I would make the
case that the media are currently being "manipulated by Washington".
However, this topic is probably best left as fruit for another thread.

More to the point, concerning the Waco trial, are my strong beliefs
that: 

1.  The wrong people are on trial.
2.  *My* tax dollars pay for it all (including the killing of
    people who are "innocent until proven guilty").
3.  Armed agression is an inappropriate means for conflict resolution,
    irrespective of whether the agressor is an individual or the state.
4.  Armed response *is* an appropriate response to armed agression,
    and that personal security is the responsibility of the
    individual, not of self-appointed political collectives.

--Vince

